{
  "id": "zig-determinant",
  "title": "Matrix Determinant",
  "description": "Write a Zig program that computes the determinant of a 3x3 matrix.",
  "difficulty": "advanced",
  "languages": ["zig"],
  "codeTemplate": {
    "zig": "const std = @import(\"std\");\n\nfn det3(m: [3][3]i32) i32 {\n    return m[0][0] * (m[1][1] * m[2][2] - m[1][2] * m[2][1])\n         - m[0][1] * (m[1][0] * m[2][2] - m[1][2] * m[2][0])\n         + m[0][2] * (m[1][0] * m[2][1] - m[1][1] * m[2][0]);\n}\n\npub fn main() !void {\n    const m = [3][3]i32{\n        [_]i32{ 6, 1, 1 },\n        [_]i32{ 4, -2, 5 },\n        [_]i32{ 2, 8, 7 },\n    };\n    std.debug.print(\"det = {}\\n\", .{det3(m)});\n}"
  },
  "verificationTest": "output.includes('det = -306')",
  "hints": [
    "For 3x3 matrix: det = a(ei − fh) − b(di − fg) + c(dh − eg)",
    "Use a function that accepts `[3][3]i32` for a fixed-size 3x3 matrix",
    "The answer for the given matrix is -306"
  ]
}
